### Optimization Guidelines
- Use React Native Animated API
  - Prefer useNativeDriver
  - Batch with Animated.parallel
  - Share Animated.Value when possible
- Implement proper cleanup
  - Clear all subscriptions
  - Reset Animated.Value
  - Remove listeners
- Batch similar animations
  - Group state updates
  - Use composition
- Cache common animations
  - Reuse Animated.Value
  - Share interpolation configs
- Minimize JS bridge usage
  - Use native-only props
  - Batch bridge updates

### Monitoring Requirements
- Track frame rates
  - Log below 55fps
  - Monitor duration
  - Track cause of drops
- Monitor memory usage
  - Watch animation objects
  - Track value sharing
- Log animation errors
  - Capture stack traces
  - Record state at failure
- Performance profiling
  - Regular profiling runs
  - Track heavy animations
- Resource cleanup verification
  - Validate unmount cleanup
  - Check memory after battles

Remember: All animations must maintain 60fps while respecting the global state management system. Proper cleanup and resource management are critical for sustained performance. 